  "id": "COMPOUND:36014 - PROTEIN:124",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Jasplakinolide Z1 and the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 zeta chain, mediated through a series of targets. Jasplakinolide Z1 is predicted to interact with CEM-SS, which is a target of both Paeonilide and (+)-Parviflorol, and all three compounds are predicted to target the CD3 zeta chain. This indicates that multiple pathways converge on the CD3 zeta chain as a downstream target of these compounds. The scores from the different paths suggest a consistent pattern of interaction, with Jasplakinolide Z1 being a central node in the network leading to the CD3 zeta chain. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the biological network and the potential for multiple compounds to influence the same cellular target.",
